---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Sandrine Chausson" description="Personal website of Sandrine Chausson, PhD researcher in computational social science at the University of Edinburgh.">
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="py-8">
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center gap-6 mb-8">
      <img
        src="/profile.jpg"
        alt="Sandrine Chausson"
        width="160"
        height="160"
        class="w-32 h-32 sm:w-40 sm:h-40 rounded-full object-cover ring-2 ring-stone-200 flex-shrink-0"
      />
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold mb-2">Sandrine Chausson</h1>
        <p class="text-stone-500 text-lg">PhD Researcher · Computational Social Science</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-4 text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Hello! My name is Sandrine and I'm a final-year PhD student in the
        <a href="https://informatics.ed.ac.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
           class="underline decoration-stone-300 hover:decoration-stone-600 transition-colors">School of Informatics</a>
        at the University of Edinburgh, where I am part of the
        <a href="https://smash.inf.ed.ac.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
           class="underline decoration-stone-300 hover:decoration-stone-600 transition-colors">SMASH research group</a>
        and the
        <a href="https://web.inf.ed.ac.uk/ilcc" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
           class="underline decoration-stone-300 hover:decoration-stone-600 transition-colors">Institute of Language, Cognition and Computation (ILCC)</a>.
        My PhD research, supervised by <a href="https://sweb.inf.ed.ac.uk/bross3/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
           class="underline decoration-stone-300 hover:decoration-stone-600 transition-colors">Dr Björn Ross</a>, focuses on developing computational text analysis
        and data science methods for inductive social science research and applies these to investigating
        the dynamics of collective sense-making processes on social media.
      </p>

      <p>
        In parallel to my PhD, I am also a Research Associate at the University of Sheffield in the School of Information,
        Journalism and Communication, where I work with <a href="https://sheffield.ac.uk/ijc/people/academic-staff/sara-torsner" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
           class="underline decoration-stone-300 hover:decoration-stone-600 transition-colors">Dr Sara Torsner</a> on the ESRC-funded research
        project <a href="https://www.profilingimpunity.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
           class="underline decoration-stone-300 hover:decoration-stone-600 transition-colors">Profiling impunity for human rights violations against journalists: A systematic
        account of state-based harm and practices of resistance</a>.
      </p>

      <p>
        With a background in Politics, Philosophy and Economics from the University of York and
        Computer Science from Imperial College London, my technical expertise lies in applied Natural
        Language Processing using Large Language Models and Machine Learning. My research, with its
        focus on theory, mixed-methods and interdisciplinarity, contributes to the fields of sociology,
        cultural studies, political science and communication. Throughout my academic journey, I have
        collaborated with institutions such as the Alan Turing Institute, the Defence Science and
        Technology Laboratory (Dstl), the University of California Berkeley, and the Queensland
        University of Technology. I am also a dedicated educator, having worked as Teaching Fellow
        and Teaching Assistant at the University of Edinburgh, where I co-created, organised and
        delivered interdisciplinary social data science related MSc courses at the Edinburgh Futures
        Institute and supervised several undergraduate and master's students.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="border-stone-200 my-10" />

  <!-- Featured project teaser -->
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-4">Featured project</h2>
    <a href="/projects/allergen-map"
       class="block border border-stone-200 rounded-lg p-5 hover:border-stone-400 hover:bg-white transition group">
      <h3 class="font-medium group-hover:text-stone-600 transition-colors mb-1">
        UK Allergen Exposure Map
      </h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">
        An interactive map of composite allergen exposure across Great Britain,
        combining tree pollen species (birch, alder, hazel), grassland, plane trees,
        and air pollution. Personalise the weights to match your own sensitivities.
      </p>
      <span class="text-sm text-stone-400 mt-3 inline-block group-hover:text-stone-600 transition-colors">
        Explore →
      </span>
    </a>
  </section>
</Base>
